Q: Seams between images when adding multiple images in a loop A: <p>I have a similar problem, I want to create a tiled background with Konva. I use fillPatternImage/fillPatternRepeat, and I don't get seams.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>import Konva from 'konva';

const stage = new Konva.Stage({
    container: 'container',
    width: window.innerWidth,
    height: window.innerHeight,
});

const layer = new Konva.Layer();
stage.add(layer);

const imageObj = new Image();
import url from './tile.png'
imageObj.src = url;

map = new Konva.Rect({
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,    
    fillPatternImage: imageObj,
    fillPatternRepeat: 'repeat',
});
layer.add(map);
</code></pre>

